        "proof_strategy": "Define zeta_G(s) = prod_{lambda in spec(A_G)} (1 - lambda^{-s})^{-1} for directed graph G with adjacency matrix A_G. Prove: zeta_G has all non-trivial zeros on Re(s) = 1/2 iff G is Ramanujan (|lambda| <= 2 sqrt(d-1) for all eigenvalues). Step 1: show zeta_G(s) = det(I - A_G * p^{-s})^{-1} where p is a formal variable. Step 2: zeros of zeta_G on Re(s) = 1/2 correspond to eigenvalues on the circle |lambda| = sqrt(d-1). Step 3: Ramanujan condition ensures all eigenvalues lie within the spectral gap. Test: compute zeta_G for Ramanujan digraphs (Lubotzky-Phillips-Sarnak construction) and verify all zeros are on Re(s) = 1/2.",
