        "description": "Conjecture: Let F be a ReLU network with rational weights and biases, and let L(x) be its rational piecewise-polynomial loss on Q^n. There exists a finite exceptional set of primes S such that for every p not in S, the sublevel-set filtration of L over Q_p has the same persistent Betti numbers in degrees 0 and 1 as the tropical active-set complex of F, after an explicit valuation-threshold rescaling. Test: Compute the active-set complex symbolically from the rational network, then for many non-exceptional primes p sample p-adic sublevel sets and compare their persistence barcodes in degrees 0 and 1 against the tropical prediction; a single infinite family of counterexamples refutes the conjecture. Impact: This would create a new bridge between neural network geometry, tropicalization, and p-adic topology, yielding arithmetic invariants of loss landscapes and potentially new tools for certified robustness and architecture diagnostics.",
