        "id": "fd_0350",
        "title": "p-Adic Universality of Gradient Dynamics in Rational ReLU Networks",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists a fixed finite set of primes P such that for every ReLU network with rational weights and every rational initialization x0 avoiding activation hyperplanes, if gradient descent on the squared loss converges over the reals to a non-degenerate local minimum, then for all primes p not in P the same update map defines a well-posed p-adic dynamical system whose orbit enters a periodic attractor determined solely by the eventual active-set sequence of the real trajectory. Test: Compute exact rational gradient-descent iterates for families of small rational ReLU networks, track their active-set sequences over the reals, and compare with p-adic iterations modulo increasing powers of p for many primes; the conjecture is refuted by infinitely many good primes exhibiting incompatible attractor structure or dependence on more than the active-set sequence, and supported if attractor type stabilizes outside a finite exceptional set. Impact: This would create a new arithmetic-dynamical invariant of neural training, linking optimization, piecewise-linear geometry, and local-global phenomena, and could enable prime-based certificates for training stability classes.",
