        "id": "fd_0360",
        "title": "Phase-Locking of Proof Search Under p-adic Valuation Features",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists a natural family of arithmetic theorem-proving tasks over polynomial, divisibility, and congruence identities such that augmenting a proof-search system with p-adic valuation annotations of intermediate expressions causes a sharp algorithmic phase transition: for infinitely many task sizes n, the median proof length drops from superpolynomial in n to polynomial in n, while the same system without valuation features does not exhibit such a drop. Test: Construct benchmark families where hidden invariants are controlled by v_p information; compare proof-search complexity with and without p-adic feature channels in a formally specified prover or tactic engine. The conjecture is refuted if no infinite family shows an asymptotic separation, and supported if one can exhibit and verify such a family with measured complexity scaling. Impact: This would identify number-theoretic local invariants as a new universal compression primitive for automated reasoning, linking arithmetic geometry, proof complexity, and ML-guided theorem proving.",
