        "id": "fd_0364",
        "title": "Adelic Echoes in Persistent Laplacians",
        "description": "Conjecture: There exists an explicit infinite family of finite simplicial complexes {K_n} with uniformly bounded local degree such that the persistent combinatorial Laplacian spectra of K_n over Q fail to distinguish the family, but the collection of spectra over finite fields F_p determines infinitely many pairwise non-isomorphic members; equivalently, for infinitely many n != m, all rational persistent Laplacian barcodes of K_n and K_m agree while the set of primes p for which the mod-p persistent Laplacian has an extra zero eigenvalue differs. Test: Construct candidate families from complexes with identical rational homology persistence but different torsion persistence, then compute persistent Laplacian spectra over Q and over F_p for many primes; the conjecture is confirmed if rational spectra coincide while mod-p spectral signatures separate infinitely many cases, and refuted if mod-p spectra never add separating power beyond rational persistence on the family. Impact: This would reveal a new prime-sensitive spectral invariant for topological data analysis, linking Hodge theory, torsion, and arithmetic structure, and could enable arithmetic-aware shape descriptors invisible to standard real-valued spectral methods.",
