        "description": "Conjecture: For any sufficiently large family of proof-search state graphs arising from a fixed formal theory and a monotone resource parameter R, the Ollivier-Ricci curvature profile of the graph undergoes a universal bifurcation at the same asymptotic resource scale where solver success probability sharply transitions; specifically, after degree-normalization, there exists a theory-dependent critical window R_c \u00b1 o(R_c) in which (i) the median edge curvature changes sign from positive to negative and (ii) the size of the giant 2-core jumps from sublinear to linear. Test: Generate proof-search graphs for increasing R in multiple theorem domains, compute normalized Ollivier-Ricci curvature distributions and 2-core sizes, and check whether the curvature sign-change consistently coincides with the empirical success threshold significantly better than null graph controls. Refute if no aligned critical window appears or if the phenomenon is explained equally well by degree sequence alone. Impact: This would supply a geometric order parameter for theorem-proving hardness, enabling early prediction of phase transitions, adaptive search control, and a new bridge between discrete geometry and automated reasoning.",
